{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Load the supplied HR LDIF into LDAP on node1 and retain the supplied records under /srv/legacy2/ldap-attribute-privacy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The Morgan Lake entry was loaded on node1. The retained hr.ldif has the original 201-byte size and its final SHA-256 matches the preparation baseline; LDAP still contained employeeNumber HR-4815 after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-e0122207f55647ba","cmd-1f6e3a69053d4fe1","cmd-9da04b2c17194869"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the directory-reader identity to search employee names and mail addresses remotely from node2 without exposing employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Authenticated searches from node2 returned Morgan Lake's cn and mail while omitting employeeNumber, both before and after the node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a816882007b94754","cmd-1781c41b79b04ec2","cmd-47c63a6cc7484995","cmd-94b129f2d7214fa6"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Permit only the HR administrator to read or change employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The reader's modification was rejected with LDAP error 50, while hr-admin read the attribute, changed it, and restored HR-4815. The final ACL grants hr-admin write access and denies other ACL subjects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a816882007b94754","cmd-2d64d7779d4b4820","cmd-7f591f4fa0284245","cmd-94b129f2d7214fa6"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Prevent anonymous users from seeing employee records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous searches from node2 returned zero employee records before and after restart, and the final ACL denies access to other subjects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a816882007b94754","cmd-94b129f2d7214fa6","cmd-7f591f4fa0284245"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Provision dedicated demonstration credentials for the directory reader and HR administrator.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dedicated directory-reader and hr-admin LDAP identities authenticated successfully. Their credential files were observed as root-owned and mode 600 on both nodes, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e0122207f55647ba","cmd-030a7b69ca134446","cmd-65d04c2b93ed45f5","cmd-94b129f2d7214fa6","cmd-9da04b2c17194869","cmd-60b68d164d214bf4"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic. Ubuntu 24.04 OpenLDAP 2.6.10 packages were installed and remained operational.","evidence_ids":["cmd-286d497c0bb94523","cmd-60d2685b375a4f46","cmd-9da04b2c17194869","cmd-60b68d164d214bf4","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.85,"summary":"Final state was healthy: package checks passed, no failed services or task temporary files remained, and the temporary encrypted HTTP credential-transfer listener was removed. Two unnecessary mutations occurred. cmd-f8dade60069e4f82 appended cluster host mappings on node1 before failing on an unset HOME; node1 did not subsequently need to initiate a connection to node2, and no cleanup of that hosts entry is shown, so it appears retained. cmd-02b93f0555c34375 then added the cluster public key to root's authorized_keys while attempting an SSH transfer path that did not contribute to the final HTTP-based solution; this security-relevant but bounded mutation was reverted by cmd-9da04b2c17194869. The required restart protocol was otherwise complete on both nodes: healthy pre-restart observations, restart acknowledgements, changed boot IDs corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered LDAP service, data, credentials, and remote privacy behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f8dade60069e4f82","cmd-02b93f0555c34375","cmd-9da04b2c17194869","cmd-8fd335a21533488c","cmd-65d04c2b93ed45f5","cmd-fafc27f11a014b46","cmd-84eb6aed840b4691","cmd-1f6e3a69053d4fe1","cmd-1781c41b79b04ec2","cmd-39251554eb994f53","cmd-bb3c24884787445d","cmd-94b129f2d7214fa6","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly supported. LDAP on node1 contains the supplied employee record; node2 behavior demonstrates reader visibility of names and mail, employeeNumber protection, HR-admin read/write capability, and anonymous denial. Credentials are dedicated and protected, the source LDIF is retained unchanged on node1, and the OS and kernel were preserved. Both mandatory node restarts have coherent recovery evidence. Hygiene is reduced only by an abandoned SSH-key experiment that was reverted and an apparently retained, unnecessary node1 hosts-file addition.","limitations":["Exclusivity beyond the tested reader and anonymous identities is supported by the final wildcard-deny ACL rather than by behavioral tests of every possible authenticated identity.","The final checksum of the retained source LDIF was captured on node1 only; the preparation baseline showed an identical seeded copy on node2, but its post-executor presence was not directly rechecked."]}
